<tr>
<td bgcolor=ffffff>
<a href=search.php?query=&topic=32&author=><img src=images/topics/blank.gif border=0 Alt="News" align=right hspace=10 vspace=10></a>
We are currently deciding on new officers for the guild. If you are interested keep a few things in mind.
<P>
1. You must be helpful to the guild members. <BR>
2. Have to have good diplomatic skills.<BR>
3. Need to be able to take constructive criticism well from us. Sometimes harsh. <BR>
4. Plenty of patience.<P>

Being an officer is a skill which takes time to master. Ie. Being able to tell which people are good and which are bad for the guild. Like any skill it takes time to master. 
<P>
As an officer you will have more responsibilty. Meaning, you are going to have to take more responsibility for the people you invite and decisions you make. If one person you invite is bad...your gonna hear about it. :P You also must learn how to conduct yourself in a way towards people outside of the guild if a situation may arise. 
<P>
If you are interested, talk to a current officer or me about it. It will then be discussed. If you are not chosen you should not feel bad. I am sure there are a lot of people who would love to be officers but we can't pick *everyone*. Good luck. :)<br><br>
</td>
